<div class="about-intro">
  <p class="about-info-short">
    Build I.T. is a hands-on technology club focused on building practical IT skills through projects, experimentation,
    and collaboration.
  </p>

  <div class="dual-card-grid">
    <CardGrid>
        <Card title="Learn by doing" icon="puzzle"> Break things, find the problem, fix it, keep building.</Card>
        <Card title="All skill levels welcome" icon="approve-check">
        No experience, knowledge, or special equipment required.
        </Card>
    </CardGrid>
  </div>

  <!-- <div class="about-callout">
    <p class="about-tagline">Learn by doing. Break things, find the problem, fix it, keep building.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="about-callout">
    <div class="about-welcome">
      <strong>All skill levels welcome.</strong>
      <span>No experience, knowledge, or special equipment required.</span>
    </div>
  </div> -->

  <p class="about-info-long">
    The Build I.T. Club at the University of Maryland exists to foster a hands-on learning environment where students
    can explore system administration, networking, virtualization, cybersecurity, self-hosting, and other IT-related
    skills. The club aims to build a supportive community where students of all skill levels can collaborate and
    experiment in a curiosity-driven environment, gaining practical, real-world experience that supports both academic
    growth and professional development. Through workshops, peer mentorship, and shared resources, the Build I.T. Club
    encourages innovation, self-reliance, and a deeper understanding of how computing systems work from the ground up.
  </p>

  <!-- <a class="faq-link" href="/faq/"> Frequently Asked Questions → </a> -->
</div>
